{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3745db136312b68cb39333b6f9539ad8882c82a20a2d1ad0bf7b757e9a07c9ea","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2ea5435565f079fbbcddb53af7e0830ab3ddea59bac3e6dc73cf6be8853d4a3b","slc_f1b67675db455d77ed2f782989e08e68850b2a14a96d1a02962b542d1454fc74"],"source_ids":["src_754ec9c4306750ea870916b123fe40af"],"text":"Repository development practice: the README points contributors to CONTRIBUTING.md for setup, tests, CI checks, coding standards, and pull request expectations, and CI badges cover test, prompt-length, and ci-checks GitHub Actions workflows.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_460bc4a7c85cc5208096c198c47fa9c8b388d8da580cc30c8842d7c8b7ea5b72","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_24787b37347f3b9a4561b9a699d9f60040ddceb036b75f4a1e5e791e65dd793a","slc_2f1f171dcdf9769fd7ce78af18f1f704444a9e8c25d2fedf4c5607cd3e1d18fd","slc_ee9cb961d9ffd747d30c3aa52ebbd3d9b503194ad4c671a28f085b17d46bf8a2"],"source_ids":["src_d65b8c7a2698566bb97fdfe51972a23a"],"text":"Configuration merges a global config (~/.herm/config.json, holding API keys, model, exploration, tool config, UI preferences) with a project-level .herm/config.json that can override model and tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_46f2b966e1746f8d27133217200ad2398e2a57f4088e6650b3caf89747da31fc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_75fee0cd1bd5046dc511aec136d326c2b9ee244c4be0735dd0a73ab1df6ec69f"],"source_ids":["src_754ec9c4306750ea870916b123fe40af"],"text":"The CLI supports multiple providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Grok, OpenRouter, Ollama, Azure OpenAI, Vertex AI, Bedrock) and models can be mixed, e.g. a different model for the main agent, exploration, or vision.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_51aa9be651617cb21e2f3882bff59532613a07a06d17d3e04efc7f2631d31630","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15219a8e88d13914dee09116084aa68459d2532a25ea3a118c9c6fc381962b5c","slc_8b187473a8ef6cb755695df44477d600c94c1f35db115a72f2cb08c26753c540","slc_e2745557b07f5f5ef69b690cc106dc06cc20004c57607732263190c7d53fb54a"],"source_ids":["src_d65b8c7a2698566bb97fdfe51972a23a"],"text":"The CLI is a terminal TUI with an event loop selecting on stdin, agent events, and async results; agent events include Thinking, ToolCall, Approval, and Done, and sub-agent events continue to be drained after the main agent stops.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6c25410aa4145661b46467d1e9135cf0aec4e4d2d82efaca0f242da2c8c57173","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_560c23b285b8ed866d51782f60cdbe0a865105112589df123b7bd264b5445386"],"source_ids":["src_754ec9c4306750ea870916b123fe40af"],"text":"Herm is described as a model-agnostic, general-purpose AI agent built for safe, flexible execution, natively supporting multiple isolation methods including containers, in-process Unix-like sandboxes, and host sandboxes such as sandbox_exec on macOS or bubblewrap on Linux.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8f807df959a3eb7fd4db477965219320e493f8917fc87958dafd653ae9f6ac59","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_46bbeb937bab796dded7809b0834d5d783c2ee28620539039d80ef4738bd0d34","slc_cb2eed1b86c9740bbb91ec685cfa31e9fc548a02a301fd3fed3f9d74fbae1e52"],"source_ids":["src_754ec9c4306750ea870916b123fe40af"],"text":"The repository also contains a SwiftUI iOS/macOS app that uses an in-process Unix-like sandbox and a Luau-scriptable runtime for on-device tasks; it is not usable as a coding agent in that context and is not yet on the App Store.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_980fd1e6782178c00af303b83b33d0c86f9200650be8081bf8168062765eecd0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03d7c653327bcc0f55778e05bfc0b7574a66fd6047bbc0b966605fab3936e982","slc_19276a1f6c962fbd37896918bfacc5a4075209fcb49c40471379bbd443f6dcf5","slc_736b752b6023fcb076324ce293a3cb854d78bef9fa2ae95463f0ef2b0bff052a","slc_ef4c465ecdb8c66c79111fd449844085842b4794f78bb3c5f74a737a8d0643c6"],"source_ids":["src_6e2703f6896d543b8899a9e5944e28f0","src_754ec9c4306750ea870916b123fe40af"],"text":"Building from source requires Go 1.24+ and, for the default container backend, Docker; the repo uses git submodules (langdag for LLM client/orchestration and cpsl for the native sandbox backend) that must be initialized before building.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a75511beb25b34f32b212d997afee17d4c6dc290d70d1abe5580445c5012d57e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bb234f3ee00e7a835dafe177fd24b4d43b4adbf1ae4da00d043746c293a5464d","slc_ce5b98b7ded5cb350765bb6551dbbac665473f4c57e56880f9e30ff9bf2740ca"],"source_ids":["src_754ec9c4306750ea870916b123fe40af"],"text":"By default the CLI runs the agent inside Docker containers that can only access files from the current working directory, with no permission prompts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f9b26289654df7b531464da0042f0bdc5515e4be9583255bc60dea59a9746a5f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"aduermael/herm@4bcb16ba05da snapshot de79735aea23feee","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_423cbf9a08ddd73a60d604931c3ed312c68bf7a93da478c60e511c56a2b8b990"],"source_ids":["src_6e2703f6896d543b8899a9e5944e28f0"],"text":"In --naked host mode, commands run through a workspace-scoped sandbox requiring sandbox-exec (macOS) or bwrap (Linux); new command segments and outside-workspace paths prompt for approval, and approved permissions persist in .herm/permissions.json with user-editable command_regexes and path_regexes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:29:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ca6c887161cf4a738d02aa4998020e48"}
